  "title": "The Shopping Bag’s Hidden Timeline",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "environment/ecology",
  "premise": "A shopper wants to compare two bags, but the picture at checkout hides production, repeated use, and disposal. A boundary slider exposes which lifecycle stages are included before any environmental comparison is made.",
  "hook": "Which parts of this bag’s life did the comparison leave out?",
  "visible_action": "Two bags unfold into timelines; a movable analysis window includes or excludes production, use cycles, and end-of-life stages.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Environmental comparisons depend on boundaries, assumptions, use, and local end-of-life conditions.",
  "gate": "Use reviewed lifecycle sources before quantitative or purchase claims; do not declare a universal winner.",
